Seems to be the way that fans in Alpha systems have tchos built into 
them which makes them hard to replace.  This has come up before.

I suspect you can buy replacements at a price, but if you've got a 
scope, it may be possible to see what signals are required from the fan 
speed sensor and spoof it.

I don't know anything about the 4000, but from memory, the 2100 shuts 
down if any of the fans stop rotating.  This 'functionality' has gone 
from my machines now that the original power supplies have been replaced 
with ATX units, giving me a lot more cheap and perhaps quieter cooling 
options.


Cheers, J/.
