>      Please append a correct "root=" boot option.
>      Kernel panic: VFS: Unable to mount root fs on 08:01
>
> I've probably missed something really stupid and obvious, but after 20
> minutes head scratching couldn't work it out.
>
> If the error report comes from the kernel, I guess the aboot.conf file
> must be found correctly, and the kernel is getting loaded from the
> correct disk and partition.  Why then, the problem mounting sda1,
> which is after all the same partition as the kernel is already loading
> from ?

Your problem is most likely caused by a missing SCSI driver in the
kernel.  Where the kernel is loaded from is irrelevant, since
obviously something else (aboot) must do the loading.  Aboot uses SRM
calls to read the disk, and works with anything supported by SRM.

Boot the livecd again, and double-check your kernel configuration.
Many Alpha machines have a Qlogic ISP1020/1040 or Symbios/NCR SCSI
controller.

