Old Alpha machines often come with what was once a high-end, very
expensive graphics card.  The problem with these cards is that driver
support in Linux is rare, and the hardware is no longer particularly
impressive.  I'd probably replace it with an ATI or Matrox card.  A
potential problem with replacing graphics cards in Alpha machines is
that SRM might not recognize the new card, and you'll have to boot in
darkness.  XFree86 should work with any supported card.

