>> Anybody know anything good for cleaning old decomposed dust out from
>> between SMT chip pins ?

>I'm sure there's something in a spray can available.

These contact sprays are IMHO the very last resort. They tend to more harm
then good. The best method to clean old machines from dust and dirt I found
is a bit more work:

1. disassemble everything
2. vacuum
3. clean boards and RAM with alcohol, for other parts, like the power supply,
take a brush in combination with a strong vacuum cleaner. Take a tooth brush
for the inside of the RAM slots.
4. dry
5. assemble
6. be happy ;-)

This has worked for me for a DEC 5000/240, which had a lot of dust in RAM
slots and was getting ECC errors all over the place.

HTH,
