On 2004-12-23, Japie <japie@deserver.nl> wrote:
> From specs. I found I allready know that the thing is way to big for the
> place it has to stand, so I have to strip it down and place it in a new
> housing.

Good luck. It's not a standard AT/ATX form factor by a long stretch.

> The machine contains 512Mb. of ram, does it take only ECC or can I use
> also non-ecc memory? (I'll bet not)

It takes a special memory board that's not compatible with anything else.
You can't just stuff PC memory in it.

> It has one 300Mhz. cpu but has room for a second, can I use any 300 as
> second or do I have to watch at things like "stepping"? (like with dual
> intel stuff)

You need another processor board of the same type as your original one.
There's one exception: If the original CPU is a B3002-AB, you can use a
B3004-BA in the same system with it, although you can't treat it as an EV56
(the software cannot guarantee which CPU it will run on, so you must only
use the EV5 features of the B3002-AB). This may take a firmware update to
get running; updating the firmware is a Good Idea in any event.


