Japie:

Here's your first mistake.  You must understand that this is an Alpha we 
are talking about, not just another vanilla box replacement for your 
PeeCee.
It's an entirely different species of computron.

The Mobo won't fit into any standard PeeCee box.
The power supply is *specific* for this system. It's got different 
plugs, extra wires, and is much more robust than anything that *ever* 
went into a PeeCee.
There's a good reason that this system uses SCSI devices, they work and 
they don't fail (well, not all that often...).
*REAL* operating systems run quite nicely on this system for a 
long_long_long time without ever needing rebooting.
Memory and processors will be expensive 'cuz there weren't a lot of 
these made, compared to PeeCee's.
Not a lot of companies could afford them, or needed their superior 
number crunching capabilities.

Make room for it in all of it's glory.  People will ask you what the 
heck it is.  Tell 'em it's a nuclear reactor or an alien artifact from 
Area 51. Tell 'em it's a Cray XMP Supercomputer (they won't know what 
that was either).  Whatever.

My 0.02

TC



