The BIOS emulation in the SRM console was done purely as a way to do generic
text console.  I asked them for an Int 10 emulation at some point - because
I was so tired of trying to figure out how to reverse engineer a device
initialization.  But I never ended up using it.

A lot of x86 BIOS code is really, really bad.  Vendors took every liberty
they could find.  So the BIOS emulation seemed to be a job of fixing things
as they went.



