Sounds like it's getting caught in the 'tryiing to configure too much'
loop. It will fail to configure something due to some missing package or
other, then go round and round in circles until forever comes.

I'd go along with the 'hold off with updates until good network in place',
that might well help. My other suggestion would be to do the minimal
possible install during the first install, then add packages carefully
once things are up and running. I've found that to be a safer if somewhat
more tedious route.




